WEBVTT

00:00:00.200 --> 00:00:08.200
Prompt injection is a major LLM application security risk where user-controlled or external input alters model behavior in unintended ways.

00:00:08.420 --> 00:00:15.540
It can be direct, where a user enters manipulative instructions, or indirect, where external content influences the model later.

00:00:15.760 --> 00:00:21.040
The greatest risks occur when LLMs can access sensitive data or trigger actions through tools.

00:00:21.260 --> 00:00:23.740
Defenses should not rely on prompting alone.

00:00:23.960 --> 00:00:34.760
Stronger approaches include trust-boundary design, least privilege, restricted tools, user approval for sensitive actions, output validation, logging, monitoring, and ongoing testing.
